# Mobile Command Center Setup Walkthrough

I have successfully executed the implementation plan and set up the foundation for the CIRO Mobile Command Center.

## Changes Made

### 1. Dependencies
- Ran `npx expo install firebase react-native-maps @react-navigation/native @react-navigation/native-stack react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context` in the `ciro-mobile` directory. The installation was successful.

### 2. Scaffolded Files
- **`firebaseConfig.js`**: Created a secure template for Firebase initialization using the v9 modular SDK. *You will need to manually fill in the `firebaseConfig` keys before running the app.*
- **`App.js`**: Overhauled the default Expo entry point to use React Navigation's Native Stack, setting `MapDashboard` as the initial route.
- **`MapDashboard.js`**: Scaffolded the primary screen. It currently renders a full-screen `MapView` centered on Islamabad and includes a UI overlay showing counts. Crucially, it sets up two `useEffect` hooks running `onSnapshot` listeners on the `ActiveCrises` and `Resources` Firestore collections, logging the incoming live data to the console.

## Next Steps
Before starting the app, please open `d:\CIRO\ciro-mobile\firebaseConfig.js` and paste in your Firebase project's web/client configuration keys.

Once that's done, review the scaffolded code. If you approve, we can move on to plotting the custom map markers!
